   "text": "I read the structure in segments and wrote each as SMILES, then joined them. Stereochemistry follows the natural auristatin and pyrrolobenzodiazepine (PBD) configurations rather than being re-derived from every wedge in the image.\n\n**Left end and central branching nitrogen**\n- The left end is a propiolamide: HC\u2261C\u2013C(=O)NH\u2013(CH2)3\u2013C(=O)\u2013N.\n- That nitrogen carries two identical \u03b2-alanine-type arms, each CH2CH2C(=O)NH\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013C(=O)\u2013.\n\n**Upper arm (to the auristatin payload)**\n- The arm continues \u2013NH\u2013CH(CH3)\u2013C(=O)\u2013NH\u2013(CH2)3\u2013C(=O)\u2013 (the alanine is drawn with plain bonds, so no stereo).\n- It then runs into the peptide N(Me)-Val\u2013Val\u2013N(Me)-dolaisoleuine (sec-butyl, OMe)\u2013proline-based dolaproine (OMe, CH3)\u2013Phe-OMe.\n- I took the Val, Phe, proline, dolaisoleuine and dolaproine centres as the natural L/auristatin configurations.\n\n**Lower arm (to the PBD dimer)**\n- The arm continues \u2013C(=O)\u2013NH\u2013CH(iPr)\u2013C(=O)\u2013NH\u2013CH2\u2013C(=O)\u2013 (L-Val), ending on the N10 nitrogen of the first PBD unit.\n\n**PBD dimer**\n- The first PBD unit has the N10 amine bonded to a CH2 (C11) rather than an imine. It carries a lactam, an exocyclic methylene on the pyrrolidine, and an aryl OMe.\n- The two aromatic rings are joined through O\u2013(CH2)5\u2013O linkers, which I counted as five carbons.\n- The second PBD unit keeps the N=CH imine, the lactam, the exocyclic methylene and an aryl OMe.\n- Both C11a centres come out as S with the stereo marks in the SMILES below.\n\nSMILES: C#CC(=O)NCCCC(=O)N(CCC(=O)NCCOCCOCCC(=O)NC(C)C(=O)NCCCC(=O)N(C)[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H]([C@@H](C)CC)[C@H](OC)CC(=O)N1CCC[C@H]1[C@H](OC)[C@@H](C)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1ccccc1)C(=O)OC)CCC(=O)NCCOCCOCCC(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)NCC(=O)N1C[C@@H]2CC(=C)CN2C(=O)c2cc(OC)c(OCCCCCOc3cc4N=C[C@@H]5CC(=C)CN5C(=O)c4cc3OC)cc21"
